---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Past continuous · A2 Grammar · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "past-continuous",
  "level": "A2",
  "topic": "Past continuous",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Describe what was happening at a past moment and set the scene for real stories: I was working at nine , Were you sleeping? , and I was cooking when the phone rang.",
  "sequence": 2,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a2-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 2</p>
  <h1>Past continuous <em>was / were doing</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Describe what was happening at a past moment and set the scene for real stories: <span class="ex">I was working at nine</span>, <span class="ex">Were you sleeping?</span>, and <span class="ex">I was cooking when the phone rang.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">past actions in progress</span>
    <span class="tag">was / were + verb-ing</span>
    <span class="tag">when / while</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare one long action with one short action.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Build was and were with verb-ing.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose forms, join clauses with when and while, and fix errors.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Tell what was really happening in your day.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">The past continuous paints the background of a story. It shows what was already in progress when something else happened.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was">was</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="finished">finished</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="finish">finish</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at the office late last night. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(was / were)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Right now, she <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> talking to a client. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(present continuous)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="finished" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the project last Friday. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(past simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One evening, three actions</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Last night at nine, Marta was cooking dinner. Her phone rang. She turned off the stove and answered."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which action was already in progress at nine?</li>
      <li>Which actions started and finished quickly?</li>
      <li>Which two words work together in <span class="ex">was cooking</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the pattern</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the subject to choose <b>was</b> or <b>were</b>, and remember the verb-ing form.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was">was</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wasn’t">wasn’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="weren’t">weren’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="working">working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="worked">worked</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> watching the news at ten.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> waiting for the bus.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>He was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the report at midnight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> raining at seven this morning.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wasn’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> listening, so she missed the question.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="weren’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sleeping; we were still at the office.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: was / were + verb-ing</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Use <span class="ex">was</span> with <strong>I / he / she / it</strong>. Use <span class="ex">were</span> with <strong>you / we / they</strong>. The main verb always takes <span class="ex">-ing</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>I / he / she / it</th><th>you / we / they</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>positive</b></td><td>I was working.</td><td>They were working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>negative</b></td><td>She wasn’t working.</td><td>We weren’t working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>question</b></td><td>Was he working?</td><td>Were you working?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Short answers: <span class="ex">Yes, I was. / No, they weren’t.</span> Do not repeat the verb-ing form in a short answer.</p>

  <h3>Why was and were do the grammar work</h3>
  <p>You already know this logic. In the present simple, <span class="ex">do / does</span> carries the grammar. With possession, <span class="ex">have / has</span> carries it. Here, <span class="ex">was / were</span> is the moving part: it agrees with the subject, moves in front for questions, and combines with <span class="ex">not</span>. The verb-ing form never changes.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Follow the moving part</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She was sleeping. → Was she sleeping? → She wasn’t sleeping.</span></p>
    <p>Only <span class="ex">was</span> moves or becomes negative. This is why <span class="ex">Did you were sleeping?</span> mixes two different systems and is not the target form.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: in progress at a past moment</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The past continuous points at a past moment and says: at that moment, the action was already happening. It had started, and it had not finished. That is why it is perfect for painting the background of a story.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>use</th><th>example</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>in progress at a past time</b></td><td>At nine, I was driving home.</td><td>The drive had started and had not finished at nine.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>setting the scene</b></td><td>The sun was shining, and people were walking to work.</td><td>This describes the situation around a story.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>two parallel actions</b></td><td>I was cooking while he was setting the table.</td><td>Both long actions were in progress together.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">You already know the verb-ing spelling from the present continuous: <span class="ex">make → making</span>, <span class="ex">sit → sitting</span>, <span class="ex">study → studying</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose was, were, or the verb-ing form</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the subject first. Then choose the word that completes the past continuous.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was">was</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wasn’t">wasn’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="weren’t">weren’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="making">making</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="made">made</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="having">having</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had">had</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>At nine last night, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> still working at my desk.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The kids <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sleeping, so we spoke quietly.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Sorry, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wasn’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> listening. Can you say that again?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>At six, she was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="making" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dinner for her parents.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We were <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="having" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> coffee on the balcony at sunrise.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> snowing at seven this morning.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="weren’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> working yesterday; the office was closed.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sitting next to me at the meeting, remember?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The heart of it: background plus interruption</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Real stories combine both past tenses. The past continuous is the long background action. The past simple is the short action that happens inside it. <span class="ex">When</span> and <span class="ex">while</span> join the two parts.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>part</th><th>tense</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>background (longer action)</b></td><td>past continuous</td><td>I was cooking dinner.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>interruption (shorter action)</b></td><td>past simple</td><td>The phone rang.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>joined with when</b></td><td>both together</td><td>I was cooking when the phone rang.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>joined with while</b></td><td>both together</td><td>While I was cooking, the phone rang.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One moment, two camera angles</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"While I was cooking, the phone rang."</span><br /><span class="ex">"I was cooking when the phone rang."</span></p>
    <p>Both sentences describe the same moment. <span class="ex">While</span> sits next to the long background action. <span class="ex">When</span> usually introduces the short interruption. Choose the joining word that matches the clause next to it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Verbs that stay simple</h3>
    <p>State verbs like <span class="ex">know</span>, <span class="ex">want</span>, <span class="ex">need</span>, and <span class="ex">understand</span> describe states, not activities. They do not normally take the continuous. Say <span class="ex">I knew the answer</span> and <span class="ex">I wanted coffee</span>, not <span class="ex">I was knowing</span> or <span class="ex">I was wanting</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type was, were, wasn’t, or weren’t</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use <b>was</b> with I, he, she, it. Use <b>were</b> with you, we, they. Short answers never repeat the verb-ing form.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Were" aria-label="answer 1" /> you sleeping when I called?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Was" aria-label="answer 2" /> it raining when you left home?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She <input class="answer-input" data-answer="was" aria-label="answer 3" /> cooking when the phone rang.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>We <input class="answer-input" data-answer="were" aria-label="answer 4" /> watching a movie when the lights went out.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Were you sleeping? No, I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="wasn’t" aria-label="answer 5" />. I was reading.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>They <input class="answer-input" data-answer="weren’t" aria-label="answer 6" /> listening, so they missed the announcement.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message about last night</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Hi Dana! You missed the excitement at the office yesterday. Around six, we were finishing the monthly report when the lights went out. Everyone was talking at once, and Leo was looking for a flashlight when the power came back on. We were only sitting in the dark for ten minutes, but after that, nobody was working. We packed up and went home."</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You followed a real story told with both past tenses.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="finishing the report">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What were they doing when the lights went out?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="finishing the report">finishing the report</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="going home">going home</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="having lunch">having lunch</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Leo">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Who was looking for a flashlight?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Leo">Leo</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana">Dana</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the writer">the writer</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="ten minutes">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. How long were they sitting in the dark?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ten minutes">ten minutes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an hour">an hour</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="all evening">all evening</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she was reading when the phone rang">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the story sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. Background action first, then the interruption.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="rang">rang</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="when">when</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="reading">reading</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="was">was</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="phone">phone</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="were you sleeping at midnight">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the question. Remember: were moves in front of the subject.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="sleeping">sleeping</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="were">Were</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="midnight">midnight</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="work" data-fix="I was working at nine last night." data-why="After was or were, the main verb needs -ing: was working.">
    <h3>Drill 6: after was and were</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was">was</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="work">work</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="nine">at nine</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="night">last night.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="did" data-fix="Were you sleeping?" data-why="Past continuous questions move was or were in front of the subject. There is no did in this system.">
    <h3>Drill 7: one system at a time</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="did">Did</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="were">were</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="sleeping">sleeping?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I was watching a movie. Change to she.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She was watching a movie.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> She was working late. Ask the question.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Was she working late?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> They were sleeping. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They weren’t sleeping.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Were you driving at ten? Answer yes.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Yes, I was.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> I was cooking. The phone rang. Join them with when.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I was cooking when the phone rang.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> I was cooking. The phone rang. Join them with while.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>While I was cooking, the phone rang.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Yesterday at three times:</b> Say what you were doing at three moments yesterday. <span class="ex">At seven, I was making coffee. At nine, I was answering emails.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask three <span class="ex">What were you doing at…?</span> questions. Listen and ask one follow-up question. <span class="ex">What were you doing at eight last night?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Set the scene:</b> Describe the start of your morning like the opening of a story: the weather, the street, the people. <span class="ex">The sun was shining. My neighbors were leaving for work.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A real interruption:</b> Tell about a time something interrupted you. Use <span class="ex">when</span>. <span class="ex">I was taking a shower when someone knocked on the door.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Same moment, two people:</b> Describe what you and another person were doing at the same moment. Use <span class="ex">while</span>. <span class="ex">While I was cooking, my brother was setting the table.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For an action in progress in the past, I use ______ or ______ plus the ______ form. For a question, ______ moves in front of the subject. A short interruption inside the background uses the past ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say one background sentence, one question, and one full story sentence with <span class="ex">when</span> about your real week.</p>
  </div>

